  "question": {
    "text": "An aqueous solution contains an unknown concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>. When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is added, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> just begins to precipitate. The final volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math>. The solubility product of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup></math>. What is the original concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>?"
  },
